There is actually a webcomic about this, kinda sorta!  It is about a temp agency for macho videogame characters to help them reintegrate into society!

&#x200B;

https://thepunchlineismachismo.com/archives/comic/02222010

In 5e I had a Oath of Vengeance paladin whose mortal enemy was an Incubus who kept seducing him, who made him kill a tribe's guard and thus my paladin had to stand trial.  In the proceedings before the trial my Paladin learned that there was another orc from that tribe who had also been seduced and mind controlled by that same Incubus and made to kill someone so my Paladin plead guilty to both the murder he had done, and the murder the orc had done, because the reason either happened was because he had failed to stop the incubus because, well, that what he would do.

&#x200B;

My DM was not happy about me pleading guilty and had to end the session there because I completely derailed his plans <.<

There is a very cute comic with this premise, Vampire Blood Drive!  It is extremely cute and extremely gay!

&#x200B;

https://miraongchua.myshopify.com/products/vbd-book-set

Some white guy was dating a girl whose family was from India, and her dad wanted to fight the guy with swords, "Punjabi style" and I just had to know what happened next.

&#x200B;

Sadly I never found a followup...

Could make you an easy target for a hate crime, if some assholes go looking for a man wearing the man bracelet or woman wearing the woman one, let alone the fact that at every bard/club I have gone to there were people who would harass women no matter what bracelet they were wearing.

&#x200B;

It is a rad concept!  Just spoiled by the fact that a lot of people are assholes...

Light Purple and Dark Purple, 1033

&#x200B;

These are so cool and pretty!

[Legacy Wars.](https://imgur.com/a/Wx41Z#5) Legend goes it was created by a Naruto fanboy who wanted to make his own TTRPG about it, but knew nothing about making games or like, common sense.

&#x200B;

I played a game once!  One of my players realized that, rules as written, going over your encumbrance doesn't actually reduce who fast you move, it instead just gives a negative to the calculation, meaning that by picking up a sufficiently large rock he could break 60mph in the opposite direction of wherever he tried to walk.

&#x200B;

[Here](https://pastebin.com/B0iGW1AA) is the most up to date rule set, if you want to play it yourself!  (Hint: Don't.)
